	(text "Hub copied from the Radxa Rock 5B v1.45 schematic, sheet 9 (FE1.1s, powered from 3.3 V: VDD5 has only\nits capacitors, as the hub's datasheet requires). USB-A power switch copied from sheet 27.\nHub ports: 1 and 2 = USB-A, 3 = USB 2 side of the 5G modem slot, 4 = spare.\nThe USB-A ports are USB 2.0 only. The processor's one spare USB 3 port goes straight to the modem slot;\nUSB 3 on the USB-A ports would need a USB 3 hub chip, for which the reference has no circuit.\nOne switch feeds both USB-A ports, limit 6800 / 3.4K = 2 A (the reference sets 1 A).\nLeft out: the common-mode chokes on the USB-A data pairs. ESD parts are generic substitutes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
